  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Recovery and Resilience strengthening after the prolonged drought in Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In total 225,645 vulnerable people in drought affected areas will benefit from project activities</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kalabo, Choma and Sinazongwe Districts</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Recovery and Resilience strengthening after the prolonged drought in Zambia; by the end of 2026, 225,645 vulnerable people in Kalabo, Choma and Sinazongwe are food secure, shock responsive and resilient vis-a-vis climatic hazards and disasters</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project, under the chronic criris budget of the MoFA grant, will focus on longer term support to help families to recover for the drought, and the strengthen their resilience/ coping capacity for possible next periods of drought.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zambia is hit by a long period of drought, declared a national Disaster in March 2024 by its president. Through the IFRC Emergency Appeal and through bilateral support under the MoFA grant NLRC/ ZRCS gas provide relief to affected families.</narrative>
  </description>
